body:
## Request

Expose an exchange-rate policy for applications that require source-provided rates. Keep the existing standalone behavior as the default. A no-capture build should retain currency parsing, accept caller-supplied quotes, and omit the generated rate corpus.

## Reproduction

With the published `link-calculator = "=0.24.0"` crate, add this `src/main.rs` to a new Cargo binary and run `cargo run --quiet`. The binary itself makes no network requests.

```rust
fn main() {
    let expression = "1 USD in RUB";
    println!("{:?}", link_calculator::Calculator::new().calculate_with_value(expression));
    println!("{:?}", link_calculator::Calculator::default().calculate_with_value(expression));

    let mut calculator = link_calculator::Calculator::default();
    calculator.update_rates_from_api("USD", "2026-11-17", r#"{"RUB":82.5143}"#);
    println!("{:?}", calculator.calculate_with_value(expression));
}
```

The first calculation can succeed without a quote from the host. `Calculator::new` initializes the default-rate and bundled-rate tables. The derived `Default` constructor starts with empty tables, so the second call reports the missing rate. The third case shows how a host can supply a quote before evaluation. The relevant code paths are the same in 0.22.0, which supplies Formal AI's Rust calculator. [Currency database constructor](https://github.com/link-assistant/calculator/blob/v0.24.0/src/types/currency.rs) · [Calculator and quote injection](https://github.com/link-assistant/calculator/blob/v0.24.0/src/lib.rs) · [Generated rates](https://github.com/link-assistant/calculator/blob/v0.24.0/build.rs)

## Workaround and proposed patch

Use the derived constructor and supply verified quotes with `update_rates_from_api`. This relies on how `Default` is implemented and does not tell Cargo to skip generating the rate corpus.

Add an explicit constructor or options type for an empty rate database and a default-on Cargo feature that guards the bundled data generation and inclusion. In a no-default-features build, test that parsing and same-currency arithmetic work, a cross-currency calculation fails before quote injection, and it succeeds after injection. The regular build would preserve the offline behavior added in #224.

Formal AI found this while auditing which runtime answers depend on shipped captures. [Audit issue](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/1613) · [Formal AI pull request](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/1614)
